[9987]={"'Tengo aquí una lista de solicitudes para ayudar a los miembros de la Liga de las Posadas que se encuentran lejos de casa sin el apoyo de sus hermanos amantes de la cerveza. Parece que extrañan sus bebidas favoritas, o en algunos casos ni siquiera las han probado.\
\
'Mi buen amigo Wald Artemisa es famoso por embriagarse y luego meterse en problemas. Creo que se fue a las Tierras Solitarias en una mala aventura alcohólica. No creo que sea lo suficientemente valiente como para regresar a menos que le consigas un poco de Cerveza de Thistlebelly en su barriga.\
\
'La Cerveza de Thistlebelly viene de la Mata de Hiedra. Deberías recoger un poco y llevársela a Wald, quien logró encontrarse en un lugar incivilizado llamado Ost Haer.'","'¡Ah, un poco de \\qCerveza de Thistlebelly\\q, ¿verdad? ¡Oh, maravilloso! ¡Ya puedo sentir cómo mi ánimo decae menos!\
\
'Con esa cerveza en mi estómago, no habrá criatura, grande o pequeña, que me infunda miedo. ¡Aún completaré el Desafío de la Liga!'","Recoge la Cerveza de Thistlebelly en la Mata de Hiedra en Hobbiton","Recoge una jarra de Cerveza de Thistlebelly","Lleva la Cerveza de Thistlebelly a Wald Artemisa","'Supongo que querrás empezar en la Mata de Hiedra. Es una posada famosa, en Hobbiton.'","La Mata de Hiedra se encuentra en el pueblo de Hobbiton, en la Comarca, lejos al oeste de las Tierras Solitarias. Wald Artemisa está en Ost Haer, en las Tierras Solitarias, lejos al este de la Comarca.\
\
Wald Artemisa, un hobbit de Hobbiton, siente que necesita un poco del sabor de casa si quiere continuar con su misión de completar el Desafío de la Liga de las Posadas. Te ha pedido que le lleves un poco de \\qCerveza de Thistlebelly\\q de la Mata de Hiedra en Hobbiton.","'¡Oh, cielos, aún no tienes la \\qCerveza de Thistlebelly\\q? Oh, si alguna vez quiero calmar mis nervios y alejarme de este lugar horrible, necesitaré un poco del sabor de casa. Por favor, tráeme un poco de la cerveza de la Mata de Hiedra.'","Todo un lío","Has recogido una jarra de Cerveza de Thistlebelly","¡Se acabó el tiempo!","'¡Oh, cielos, me parece que me he metido en un buen lío! ¡Un lío de verdad! Fui tan tonto al pensar que podría hacer esto por mi cuenta, y ahora estoy aquí completamente solo. Ah, pero aquí estás, quizás puedas ayudarme.\
\
'¡Oh, Dios mío, parece que me he puesto a hablar sin parar! He tenido un gran susto, así que estoy hecho polvo. Verás, soy un hobbit de Hobbiton y miembro de la Liga de las Posadas. Quería completar el Desafío de la Liga y pensé que sería una gran aventura, como la del viejo loco Bolsón. Pero parece que todo lo que he hecho es rodearme de toda clase de criaturas malvadas. Sin embargo, si tuviera un poco del sabor de casa, podría recuperar mi coraje y salir de aquí sano y salvo.\
\
'¿Podrías traerme un poco de \\qCerveza de Thistlebelly\\q de la Mata de Hiedra en Hobbiton? ¡Eso debería ser todo lo que necesito para ponerme en marcha!'","Se te ha encargado completar una entrega a un miembro de la Liga de lasPosadas que se ha quedado varado lejos del festival esta temporada.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000> NOTA: Esta misión se eliminará de tu bitácora de misiones cuando termine el festival actual. </rgb>","Has obtenido Cerveza de Thistlebelly","Devuelve la Cerveza de Thistlebelly antes de que se acabe el tiempo.","La Cerveza de Thistlebelly se puede comprar en la Mata de Hiedra, en Hobbiton.\
\
Deberías conseguir algo de Cerveza de Thistlebelly para entregársela a Wald Artemisa.","'¡Por favor, ve a la Mata de Hiedra, y date prisa! Necesito esa cerveza...'"},
[9988]={"'¡Wald Artemisa sentirá ahora la superioridad de la habilidad cervecera de los enanos! Solo debes traerle una cerveza de la Mansión de Thorin para avanzar con este plan.'","'¡Gracias, gracias, gracias! ¡La beberé ahora mismo!'\
\
Wald Artemisa bebe un gran trago de la cerveza suave.\
\
'¡Ya me siento más valiente! ¡Esta es la cerveza con mejor sabor que he probado jamás, y he probado casi todas las cervezas al oeste de las Tierras Solitarias!'","¡Se te ha acabado el tiempo!","'¿Cerveza suave? ¿Eso es todo? ¿Seguro que no quieres algo más emocionante? Bueno, si insistes, aquí tienes.'","Lleva la falsa Cerveza de Thistlebelly a Wald Artemisa","Una Verdadera Picazón","'He recibido un tipo distinto de órdenes de Jónar, el jefe de esta asociación. Odia tanto a la Liga de las Posadas que me ha asignado una tarea muy diferente de la de mi vecino de la Liga. ¡Chist, que no nos oiga!\
\
'Un pequeño hobbit llamado Wald Artemisa se lanzó a una aventura alocada en busca de notoriedad dentro de la Liga de las Posadas y ahora se ha metido en un buen lío. Desea la Cerveza de Thistlebelly, un sabor de su tierra natal, para reunir el valor necesario para salir de allí.\
\
'Pero en su lugar le llevaremos una cerveza simple y corriente. Solo una cerveza, nada más. Y para peor, será de la Mansión de Thorin. Serán los enanos quienes lo motiven con su maestría cervecera superior, y no esos bribones hobbits.'","El tabernero se encuentra en la bodega de la Mansión de Thorin.\
\
Deberías recoger una cerveza suave de la taberna de la Mansión de Thorin y luego llevársela a Wald Artemisa haciéndola pasar por Cerveza de Thistlebelly.","Has recogido la falsa Cerveza de Thistlebelly","Recoge la falsa Cerveza de Thistlebelly","Se te ha encomendado entregar cosas desagradables a miembros necesitados de ayuda de la Liga de las Posadas, algo que solo haría la peor de las ${CLASS}.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: Esta misión se eliminará de tu registro de misiones cuando finalice el festival actual.</rgb>","Wald Artemisa se encuentra en Ost Haer, en las Tierras Solitarias.\
\
Deberías llevarle la falsa Cerveza de Thistlebelly a Wald Artemisa. Lo engañarás con esto, pues en realidad se trata de una cerveza suave de la Mansión de Thorin."},
[9997]={"Arvedui has shown you and Lothrandir the hidden entrance to Agoroth in Jä-reitti.\
\
You should talk to Lothrandir.","A powerful artifact awaits in the hidden fortress of Agoroth. You must reach it before the Witch-king's forces.","Surprisingly, Lothrandir has compelled Arvedui to accompany him to the Lossoth village. Lothrandir seems to be telling Arvedui a story, and has not noticed you approach.\
\
You should listen in on their conversation.","', you return. The Lumi-väki did not expect to see you again after that business with the ring was finished. At least, not so soon. What do you want from Yrjänä?'\
\
You explain that the Angmarim are searching for a treasure in the hidden fortress of Agoroth, and that you need the key Arvedui left with the Lossoth before his death if there is any hope of beating them to it.\
\
'Yrjänä knows of what you speak. The Lumi-väki have kept this heirloom safe. But I ask, do you know the true significance of this item? It is more than a metal key to a metal door. The Lumi-väki know. My people have long memories.\
\
'The songs tell of a time long ago, when the tall men came in suits of iron. They asked the Lumi-väki for peace, and to swear an oath before a great stone, blue as the sky on a clear day. The Lumi-väki swore to help the tall men fight their enemies, and in trade, we received weapons of forged metal to fight our ancient rivals, the Gauredain. A good trade, until the Iron Men went to war. Many Lumi-väki died in foreign lands, facing enemies that were not our own.\
\
'Even still, the Lumi-väki kept our oath and the peace with the Iron Men and their descendants. One day, they came again to Sûri-kylä. They said the stone must be moved and hidden. There were other stones, with oaths made by other clans, that were taken, and corrupted. The Iron Men wished to build a new Stone-home here, in our lands. The Lumi-väki were hesitant. An enemy capable of corrupting such powerful magic is not an enemy to be made lightly. We knew who that enemy must be....\
\
'But the Lumi-väki were compelled by their oath, and allowed the Iron Men to build their Stone-home here. We hid the way with our magic, for we knew if the stone was found and corrupted, the Lumi-väki would become bound to that evil.\
\
'For many years, the Iron Men were left to their Stone-home. Rarely, one would come to Sûri-kylä to barter for supplies. Then came a foul wind carrying the scent of evil, followed by the worst storm in many generations. No more Iron Men came after that day, and we feared the stone must now be unprotected.\
\
'This key... it will unlock the door to the Oath-stone. Of this Yrjänä is certain. It will be given in trade, but not for goods or currency, no... in return, Yrjänä asks that  makes ${PLAYER:her[f]|his} own oath. Promise to the Lumi-väki that you will protect the stone from Angmar, and promise Yrjänä that you will find a way to destroy the Oath-stone for good. The Lumi-väki wish to be be bound to no-one. We will give our allegiance to those deserving, and fight enemies we understand fully.\
\
'Do you accept?'","Lothrandir and Arvedui are outside Sûri-kylä.\
\
You should listen to their conversation in 'Instance: The Power of Oaths.'","Racing to Agoroth","Complete 'Instance: The Power of Oaths'","Yrjänä nods solemnly.\
\
'A pact is made. Go to Salavahti and tell her that Yrjänä has given you Arvedui's key. She is the keeper of ancient things, and of stories from long ago. You will find her on the rise above the village.\
\
'The Lumi-väki are relying on you, ${PLAYER}. Do not fail us.'","You approach and listen in on Lothrandir and Arvedui's conversation.","Salavahti can be found on the rise above Sûri-kylä.\
\
You should talk to Salavahti.","Salavahti gives you the key of Agoroth","'It is clear we do not have much time if we are to reach Agoroth's treasure before the Angmarim. You should go ahead to Sûri-kylä and ask the Lossoth council if they will barter for the key to Agoroth. They are an honourable folk, and will make fair trade for it. Meanwhile, I would like to speak with King Arvedui at length, giving him word of the last thousand years, and to hear tales of the Dúnedain of old.'","Habla con Yrjänä","The Lossoth chieftain Yrjänä can be found in the Great Lodge of Sûri-kylä.\
\
You should ask Yrjänä if the Lossoth would be willing to trade for the key of Agoroth.","'What brings you to Salavahti, outsider?'\
\
You tell Salavahti that Yrjänä has given you the right to take Arvedui's key. Her eyes widen.\
\
'The Lumi-väki have held this key for many generations. We knew that one day someone would come for it, as they did for the ring of Arvedui. By Yrjänä's will, I offer it into your care.'\
\
Salavahti turns from you, and whispers a prayer in the language of the Lossoth. She then begins humming a single tone, deep in her chest. This tone makes the tall stone spires around you vibrate, and the snow dance, unearthing a square cut-out in the rock you would never have been able to otherwise see. She lifts the square-shaped stone, exposing a hollow space, and stops humming. Inside rests an unassuming bundle of elk-hide, worn with age. Salavahti takes the bundle and unwraps it, revealing an intricately detailed metal key. You see that the key is quite large, and the seven-pointed star of Arnor serves as its handle. This must be the key of Agoroth. Salavahti holds the key toward you, allowing you to take it.\
\
'Our business is concluded, outsider. May you do great things with this. The one known as Lothrandir has come to meet you. Salavahti sees much from this high place. You should go to him.'","<rgb=#FF0000>Agree</rgb> to Yrjänä's terms","'Arvedui has shown us the way to Agoroth. Now, we must prepare to venture inside. Let us hope we have arrived before the Angmarim!'","Yrjänä has asked you to promise to find a way to destroy the Oath-stone in exchange for the key of Agoroth.\
\
If you accept these terms, let Yrjänä know that you <rgb=#FF0000>agree</rgb>.","Talk to Salavahti","Salavahti has informed you that Lothrandir has returned to Sûri-kylä to meet you.\
\
You should talk to Lothrandir.","You agree to Yrjänä's terms in exchange for the key","Talk to Yrjänä in the Great Lodge of Sûri-kylä","You have agreed to destroy the Oath-stone in exchange for the key of Agoroth.\
\
You should talk to Yrjänä in Sûri-kylä.","Talk to Lothrandir in Jä-reitti","Talk to Lothrandir outside Sûri-kylä"},
[9998]={"Rage of the Erui","Talk to Lady Terenis in Tumladen","Deliver Castamir's armour to Angbor near the Crossings of Erui","'We will do what we must, ${PLAYER}. Are you prepared?'","'What is this armour you lay before me? An ornate piece despite such age and wear... it can be none other than the armour worn by the Usurper himself!\
\
'As much as I wish to trust your words, I cannot fathom these tales you tell of the Five Sisters... they are naught but fables told to the young. Yet, the river has held close a relic of our bloody history, and I would not dishonour our people by ignoring such a find!\
\
'I shall send this armour to Lord Sirgon and see it returned to Pelargir until this war comes to an end. Perhaps the Lady would like to hear more of your tale, but I can tarry no longer in Lebennin.'","Talk to Roamingstar, Maiden of Gilrain","'The Lone Lady...\
\
'She has always been the most distant of my Sisters, but I never sensed such darkness within her. Only a great sadness... a sadness she has carried with her for many of your years. She never spoke much to us... never even speaking of her true name, but I wish she had come to us with her troubles. We have all seen horrors in the long years we have spent in these lands - she must know that she does not stand alone!\
\
'The Men of Lebennin fought brother against brother and spilled much blood in her waters, but now you say the southern Men that seek to cross her waters are met by rotting suits of armour? I fear she will not be calmed easily, but my Sisters and I must reach her somehow.\
\
'Travel to the Crossings of Erui... for it is there that my Sisters and I shall meet you. We shall put an end to this, no matter what action must be taken!'","Lady Terenis can be found in the Great Hall of Tumladen.\
\
You have delivered Castamir's armour to Angbor, and should now speak to Lady Terenis.","Angbor can be found on a hill to the west of the Crossings of Erui.\
\
You have aided Roamingstar and her Sisters in calming the Lone Lady's rage, and have also recovered pieces of Castamir's armour. You should bring the armour to Angbor near the Crossings of Erui.","The Sisters of Lebennin seek to calm their Sister's fury before it consumes both the Enemy and the people of Gondor alike.","Roamingstar can be found in her glade in north-eastern Dor-en-Ernil.\
\
Roamingstar has rallied her Sisters and is now prepared to confront the Lone Lady. You should speak to her when you are ready.","'You speak of unbelievable things, ${PLAYER}, but you assure me that my people are safe, so I shall hold your words to be true.\
\
'This Glassiel you spoke of in Halach, she seems to be a most interesting woman and one whom I would like to speak with in time. Ah, but such things are for another day...\
\
'I have one last thing to ask of you, my friend.'"},
[9999]={"By completing this quest, you will receive a set of Raid Gear.","'Buckle up buttercup, here comes the gear!'","Raid Gear: Burglar","'Looking for some sweet raid gear are you? Well, I am the man, er dwarf to help you! I've made just about all this stuff, and while it has crushed my soul, the black lump that is my heart is warmed to see you enjoy these items.\
\
'So, if you'd like a set raid gear, speak to me again.'","Talk to Avon to continue"},
}
